# sysop-issuers — hosts permitted to ORIGINATE host-directed system ops
# (scripts/jobs/send-host-op.sh -> msgs/host/<GARDEN>, executed by sysop.sh).
#
# THIS FILE REPLACES THE DEFAULT. When absent or empty the issuer set defaults to
# the leader alone; once it has a single entry, ONLY the listed hosts may issue —
# so the leader must be listed explicitly here or it silently loses the ability.
#
# The gate governs WHO MAY SEND. It does NOT widen WHAT may be sent: the op
# vocabulary stays closed (set-workers, drain, reset-failed, restore, unit,
# deploy), each op is host-scoped to the sysop that receives it, and the two
# destructive ops (unit, deploy) additionally require maintainer attestation --
# an authorized_by: <login> on maintainers/allowlist, which no agent may
# originate. Ferry and identity switching are permanently out of the vocabulary.
#
# Added endolin-garden-ece02cb4 on 2026-08-01 at the maintainer's explicit
# instruction, so a liaison session on that follower can direct worker counts on
# peer hosts (the unattended-follower case the sysop exists for).
